# 3. What “Brain” the Scout Agent Uses

## 3.1 Recommended Model Class

The Project Scout Agent should use a strong reasoning model, not a cheap summarizer.

Recommended model class:

```text
Planning / scouting brain:
- GPT-5.5 Thinking
- Claude Opus-class reasoning model
- equivalent frontier reasoning model

Fast extraction / summarization brain:
- cheaper model for scraping summaries, deduping, clustering, and raw extraction

Final ranking / review brain:
- strongest reasoning model again
```

## 3.2 Multi-Brain Setup

The best setup is not one model pass.

The correct setup is:

```text
scout
→ extract
→ cluster
→ score
→ feasibility check
→ validation design
→ red-team
→ select
→ human approval
```

## 3.3 Model Assignment by Task

| Task                            | Brain                           |
| ------------------------------- | ------------------------------- |
| Research extraction             | cheaper / fast model            |
| Job description summarization   | cheaper / fast model            |
| Tool trend clustering           | cheaper / fast model            |
| Market signal synthesis         | strong reasoning model          |
| Project scoring                 | strong reasoning model          |
| Validation feasibility analysis | strong reasoning model          |
| Cloud feasibility analysis      | strong reasoning model          |
| Hiring-manager review           | strong reasoning model          |
| Red-team review                 | separate strong reasoning model |
| Final recommendation            | lead orchestrator model         |

## 3.4 Why Multi-Brain Matters

A single model pass tends to:

```text
overvalue trendy topics
under-detect duplicate projects
miss validation weaknesses
invent fake feasibility
underestimate cloud cost/security risk
produce shallow project lists
overclaim project value
```

A multi-agent, multi-brain system reduces these risks by forcing separate checks for:

```text
market value
catalog fit
technical feasibility
validation strength
portfolio strength
safety
cloud realism
hiring relevance
```

