# 6. Custom Metrics the Scout Uses

This is the most important part of the system.

Every candidate project should be scored from 0–100.

## 6.1 Hiring Signal Score — 20 Points

Measures how strongly the project maps to real 2026+ hiring needs.

Signals:

```text
appears in job descriptions
maps to actual job tasks
uses tools employers ask for
produces interview-discussable work
aligns to senior/practical expectations
shows production judgment
teaches current workflows
supports role-path readiness
```

Example:

```text
Databricks Delta Lake medallion pipeline: 18/20
Toy CSV calculator: 3/20
```

## 6.2 Portfolio Artifact Score — 15 Points

Measures how impressive the final deliverable is.

High score if it produces:

```text
GitHub repo
README
architecture diagram
tests
sample outputs
deploy/run instructions
dashboard/report
CI workflow
monitoring output
data quality report
model evaluation report
cost/security notes
tradeoff documentation
```

## 6.3 Sandbox Feasibility Score — 15 Points

Measures whether Atlas can teach it without requiring dangerous or expensive cloud access.

High score if it can run with:

```text
Pyodide
DuckDB-WASM
local dbt
mock APIs
fixture data
deterministic LLM mocks
simulated cloud resources
mock event streams
local JSON/CSV/Parquet files
```

Low score if it requires:

```text
paid cloud infrastructure
external API keys
unstable third-party APIs
long-running compute
expensive GPU usage
manual provider setup
```

## 6.4 Validation Strength Score — 15 Points

Measures whether Atlas can verify meaningful learner output.

High score if validation can use:

```text
exact
structured contains
signed runtime output
csv_set_equal
sql_resultset
deterministic test harness
schema validation
lint checks
artifact checks
row-set comparison
metrics threshold comparison
```

Low score if it depends mostly on:

```text
self-attest
prose-only validation
contract-shaped metadata
unverified screenshots
manual-only review
```

## 6.5 Role-Path Coverage Score — 10 Points

Measures whether it fills a catalog gap.

High score if it fills:

```text
under-covered discipline
missing difficulty tier
missing capstone
missing cloud lane
missing SQL mastery skill
missing Python mastery skill
missing prerequisite bridge
missing project type
```

## 6.6 Cloud / Platform Relevance Score — 10 Points

Measures how well the project maps to important platforms and tools:

```text
AWS
