# 8. Step-by-Step Project Identification and Selection Process

## Step 1 — Market Signal Collection

The Market Signal Agent collects signals from:

```text
job descriptions
company career pages
cloud provider role guides
tool documentation
GitHub popular repositories
industry blogs
competitor course catalogs
recruiter language
current platform gaps
emerging technology trends
```

Output:

```text
top tools
top workflows
top project patterns
repeated job phrases
emerging skill clusters
role-specific requirements
cloud/platform trends
```

## Step 2 — Atlas Catalog Gap Analysis

The Catalog Analyst Agent inspects Atlas.

It answers:

```text
How many projects exist per discipline?
How many projects exist per difficulty?
Which skills are missing?
Which providers are missing?
Which validation kinds dominate?
Which projects are too similar?
Which projects lack strong portfolio artifacts?
Which role paths lack capstones?
Which beginner-to-advanced transitions are weak?
Which disciplines lack SQL mastery?
Which disciplines lack Python mastery?
Which cloud providers are underrepresented?
```

## Step 3 — Candidate Generation

The Project Scout Agent proposes candidate projects.

For each candidate:

```text
title
slug
discipline
difficulty
scenario
tools
final artifact
validation idea
sandbox mode
BYO cloud extension
prerequisites
estimated steps
estimated time
expected role signal
```

## Step 4 — Deduplication

The Deduplication Agent checks:

```text
title overlap
slug overlap
scenario overlap
skill overlap
tool overlap
final artifact overlap
role-path redundancy
difficulty redundancy
```

It returns one of:

```text
keep
merge
rename
revise
reject
```

## Step 5 — Feasibility Analysis

The Sandbox Feasibility Agent decides:

```text
Can this run in browser?
Can it run with DuckDB-WASM?
Can it run with Pyodide?
Does it require real cloud?
Can cloud be mocked?
Does it need external API keys?
Can it be validated deterministically?
Does it require unsupported packages?
Does it require long-running compute?
Can it have a BYO-cloud extension?
```

## Step 6 — Validation Strategy Design

The Validation Architect Agent proposes:

```text
validation kind per step
server-side vs client-provisional
signed runtime evidence need
expected output format
grader gaps
test plan
rollback plan
H3 claim level
```

If validation is too weak, the project gets revised or rejected.

## Step 7 — Hiring-Manager Scoring

The Hiring Signal Agent scores:

```text
Would this project impress a hiring manager?
Can it be discussed in interviews?
Does it map to real job tasks?
Does it show practical judgment?
Does it show architecture thinking?
Does it show debugging/failure-handling?
Does it show tool fluency?
```

## Step 8 — Portfolio Scoring

The Portfolio Artifact Agent asks:

```text
Will this produce a strong GitHub repo?
Can it generate a README?
Can it generate diagrams?
Can it create evidence?
Can it be shared on LinkedIn?
Can a recruiter understand it in 60 seconds?
Can the learner explain it in an interview?
```

## Step 9 — Ranking

The Scoring Agent combines all scores.

Output:

```text
Top 10 candidates
Recommended 6 to author
Rejected list with reasons
Risks and prerequisites
Provider coverage analysis
Discipline coverage analysis
Validation coverage analysis
```

## Step 10 — Human Approval

The human operator approves:

```text
Build these 6
Revise these 2
Reject these 2
Hold these for later
```

## Step 11 — Authoring

The Project Author Agent writes hidden project modules.

Output:

```text
scripts/src/authored/<course>__<slug>.ts
```

## Step 12 — Audit

Automated audits run:

```text
typecheck
audit:authoring
audit:pedagogy
audit:difficulty-labels
validation-kind audit
copy-safety scan
BC audits if relevant
```

## Step 13 — Red-Team Review

The Red-Team Reviewer checks:

```text
overclaims
weak validation
hidden answer leakage
fake cloud claims
bad instructions
duplicate content
unrealistic time estimates
security issues
cost issues
credential issues
```

## Step 14 — Manual Publish Checklist

A human or high-trust review agent signs off.

Checklist:

```text
instructions complete
hints non-leaky
validation honest
scenario coherent
portfolio deliverable clear
difficulty reasonable
no H1/H2 overclaims
no fake cloud integration
no placeholder content
audits green
```

## Step 15 — Visibility Flip

Only then:

```text
learner_visible=true
```

